@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-share-extension-only-adapts-system-input
The extension MUST use the existing shared-domain parser and bounded canonical
codec; it MUST NOT contain account RPC, settings, Compose screens or credentials.
Saving MUST recheck the originally captured source token through the coordinated
storage after asynchronous system item loading. A replaced source MUST require a
new explicit share. Unsupported input or unavailable provisioning MUST show an
actionable error without a Save action. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native
share handoff and maximum-reuse plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] ios-share-does-not-promise-host-foregrounding
The share adapter MUST explain that saving requires the user to open Pully, then
complete the extension after Save. It MUST NOT use responder tricks, private APIs,
arbitrary extension URL opening or a misleading Open Pully control. App Group setup
MUST remain optional for the ordinary app and CI; configuration text alone MUST NOT
claim that the OS granted a shared container. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 user
mediated native share handoff and external-provisioning constraints.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-share-bundles-its-required-reason-manifest
The extension MUST bundle its own required-reason API manifest for the native
container file metadata it reads. It MUST declare access limited to its own or
App Group containers and MUST NOT adopt the host's unrelated UserDefaults reason.
Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native share storage and credential-boundary plan,
and Apple's required-reason manifest requirement for FileTimestamp APIs.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;product] ios-share-copy-uses-canonical-preferred-locales
Every extension label, status and recovery message MUST come from the canonical web
locale catalogs through the same Android mirror bundled as i18n resources. The
extension MUST use the actual preferred language, regional matching and canonical
English fallback, including a missing translated key. It MUST NOT keep a separate
translation table, persist language/account settings in the App Group or display raw
storage error descriptions. Source: root strings-from-web-locales, DESIGN.md locale
enforcement and confirmed 22 October 2026 native composition review finding 1.
